F1 — mandatory tests absent from the acceptance route (blocking)
OPERATIONAL-GOVERNANCE-CHARTER.md lines81–83 and CLAUDE.md lines64–65 require certificate self-tests in normal and python -O modes with actual field mutations. RUN-GATES.md line50 instead says “If the separate engineering auditor elects to run” and supplies only python test_validate_return348A.py. The six preproduction gates omit tests. The wrapper's typed authority fields and hash-bound receipts (lines15–33) omit test evidence. Its transport record explicitly writes predicate_corpus_rerun=false (line105). ENGINEERING-REPORT.md lines47/51 correctly discloses unexecuted tests but routes from separate audit/CI to execution without making this obligation mandatory. The five accepted /36 rejected fixture counts are predictions, not observations. A prior343 test outcome cannot discharge this changed-validator obligation.
This is not a finding that the Python predicates fail. Their explicit checks and counters appear optimization-safe on source reading. It is a documented process defect: the prepared acceptance path can omit the required actual normal/-O self-test evidence. This audit cannot convert static inspection into those executions. The blocker concerns acceptance of a certified production result, not a claim that the charter forbids creating any exploratory PDF before tests. The simplest repair is a mandatory normal-and-optimized test gate, with genuine receipts bound to the exact validator and test bytes, before production-result acceptance; preferably before the production attempt. Update inconsistent optional wording and make the parent relay enforce that gate, or provide a separately reviewed explicit mandatory acceptance workflow. Execute only in an owned authorized Colab Linux runtime; retain stdout, stderr, real exit, mode, exact hashes, measured resource observations, failures and separate stop/readback. Re-audit changed operational bytes. Do not fabricate receipts to satisfy the wrapper.
The test corpus currently checks5 positive and36 negative field cases. It does not exercise the entire real-return ZIP validator. In addition to the existing mutations, challenge wrong support hash and TeX argument, malformed source/PDF binding, missing rendered page, archive member type and payload-universe changes. Such synthetic checks must remain labelled synthetic; they are not a production artifact or evidence that a PDF was built. Absence of those extra cases is a coverage limitation/recommendation, distinct from the mandatory normal/-O blocker.

