Native exits, failures and cleanup — static design PASS with explicit limits
Native stdout/stderr are created separately, flushed and retained; actual decimal child exit is atomically published only after process wait. Explicit nonzero/timeout predicates fail; bool is not accepted as an integer zero. Before each TeX attempt, existing source/output hashes are recorded, and after it native files plus actual child record are copied even on failure. Existing native files are not proof of that pass succeeding. Spawn or I/O failure can leave partial evidence without an invented exit. Root failure trace is preserved and FAILED_PRESERVED status used. Clone deletion is limited to exact own children after resolve/symlink checks; cleanup debt forces failure. Archive creation is exclusive, raw file manifest lists exact outputs. Fatal process death or report/archive I/O failure can still prevent completion; preserved files are then debt, not a successful package.
Subprocess timeout kills the immediate process and waits; it is not proof every descendant stopped. The outer owned runtime stop/readback is still required. WSL capture waits are not globally bounded if host/WSL itself wedges, despite GNU timeout supervising CLI calls. The helper's pipe/file setup can fail before a complete sentinel. These are stated recovery limits, not fabricated universal lifecycle guarantees.

Allocation, ownership and separate closure — static design PASS, no current runtime
The wrapper refuses an existing attempt and existing own-config path or symlink before allocation. It uses the distinct tep348-build-a-own-cpu namespace/config, not another chat's runtime. attempted is set before the allocation call so a partial allocation failure still reaches stop plus independent sessions query. Allocation nonzero is explicitly rejected before readiness/build. Readiness checks exact observed JSON source/cwd/os/absence booleans; it is point-in-time readiness only. One builder call is allowed; download is attempted in its finally even on a failed builder invocation. Outer finally attempts stop and then a separate backend query independently, before report writes; query is attempted even if stop capture fails. Missing/nonzero/incomplete lifecycle sets failure. No blind retry exists.
The query's zero exit is never interpreted automatically as no active runtime. Actual backend text still needs parent inspection. A separate recovery query helper has its own output names, checks a recorded allocation request, and cannot allocate/build/stop. The Linux /content checks are environment-shape checks, not cryptographic Colab identity; ownership comes from the real authorized transport/config and backend evidence. Config absence is not an atomic cross-process lock, and literal Windows staging path validation is not a reparse-point ancestry attestation; parent must retain physical-path/exclusive-delivery discipline. Catastrophic host failure or an allocation that loses its config may need explicit recovery; no receipt here claims current348 closure. No current runtime was opened during this audit.

Return ZIP, path containment and bindings — static design PASS with test limitation F1
The actual-return caller checks actual bundle hash against an externally observed digest, freshness, single-component exact19 names, duplicates, regular-file mode, encryption prohibition and total uncompressed size bound. It extracts only that fixed set into a new Linux root with exclusive files. Validator and44-source manifest hashes are verified before import. Partial failures remain intact. The digest is an input to be captured from a real future transfer, not a synthetic constant receipt.
The inner validator rejects absolute/traversal/backslash/empty/control/reserved Windows names, case-fold duplicates, trailing dot/space names and file/parent collisions. It rejects encrypted/nonregular ZIP entries, constrains member count/size and requires manifest exact universe and raw hashes/lengths. It compares44 raw source-capture files with pinned inventory and verifies both active source hashes. It binds exact native sequence27, actual zero exits and no timeouts, TeX argv, raw head/epoch/diff logs, canonical PDF header/hash/length and both clone PDFs, source binding, native retention records, page count/PNG numbering/signature, contacts universe and coarse text completeness. Native TeX outputs include each pass's exact main/support bytes, aux/log/out/PDF files; second-pass PDF must equal canonical. Failure/debt files are forbidden and the entire returned evidence universe is exact.
The main checker checks four outer lifecycle exits; backend-readback files are included in the19-member caller set but their semantic content is not an automatic acceptance predicate. The parent readback obligation is essential and explicitly stated. Non-TeX command argv is checked for shape/sequence and relevant observed output, not every complete argv equality; parent must read actual commands/logs. Contacts membership and PNG header checks are structural, not visual/content assurance. Malformed ZIP/JSON exceptions fail closed, but no dynamic adversarial run was performed. The full package can be hundreds of MiB in RAM; this is proposed remote high-memory processing, not an authorized Windows light task.

